      "that inner war leaves men estranged from themselves, living in bodies that feel like fortresses instead of homes, treating their own emotional needs as enemies instead of messages. the promised security turns out to be an illusion: he trades real safety for the look of it, and real strength for its appearance.",
      "## but what of women?",
      "women suffer under patriarchy through objectification; men suffer through isolation. women face outside limits on their agency; men face an inside ban on vulnerability. women fight for the right to be powerful; men struggle for permission to be tender. we're hurt by the same system in different ways.",
      "these two kinds of suffering feed each other. the emotional emptiness patriarchy creates in men feeds their objectification of women, as they look for outside conquest to fill what's missing inside. and men's fear of vulnerability keeps them from really understanding what women go through, which keeps the misunderstanding and harm going. the system damages both, then uses the damage to turn possible allies into enemies.",
      "this insight— that patriarchy wounds both men and women— does not imply moral equivalence between the forms of suffering or equal distribution of systemic power. women face concrete limitations on bodily autonomy, economic opportunity, and physical safety that most men do not. yet recognizing men's genuine suffering under patriarchy opens possibilities for alliance rather than antagonism, for collaboration rather than competition in dismantling oppressive structures.",
      "## surpassing binary thinking",
      "patriarchy depends on binaries (masculine versus feminine, strong versus weak, rational versus emotional, dominant versus submissive, alpha versus omega, etc.), and that shrinks everyone by limiting how much of human experience and expression we can reach. it cuts men and women off from parts of themselves, with inner divisions that mirror the outer power structure.",
      "look at how human qualities get gendered: compassion is called feminine and ambition masculine; vulnerability feminine, stoicism masculine; nurturing feminine, protecting masculine. that split means both men and women only develop half their potential. the full human range, which includes both tenderness and strength, vulnerability and resilience, connection and autonomy, ends up available to nobody.",
      "this binary thinking particularly harms those whose gender identity or expression does not conform to patriarchal norms. transgender, non-binary, and gender non-conforming individuals face extreme sanctions for transgressing patriarchy's rigid categories, revealing through their suffering how artificial and constraining these categories truly are.",
