      "the hollowing of the Colorado River Basin in Bacigalupi's story stood for a crisis bigger than hydrology: a collapse of the covenant between humanity and nature. the river that gave life to millions was reduced to a trickle, its legal tangles a battleground. such visions used to belong to fiction. now Lake Mead and Lake Powell have fallen to levels that were unthinkable a few decades ago, and allocation has become a kind of combat, with states fighting to hold their claims over an emptying basin.",
